{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/375990-space-combat","id":375990,"title":"Space! Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-20T02:34:19-08:00","id":375990,"title":"Space! Combat","content":"So I am curious to hear what you all did with space battles, considering the normal rules (as far as I know them) are bettered suited towards fighter combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T10:14:27-08:00","id":376355,"title":"","content":"The fact that space battles are better suited to fighter combat is something we tried to take into account for Codename: Sardonyx, and I think the scaling rules work <i>really</i> well. Capital ship combat should feel appreciably different from snubfighter dogfights, while the occasion hotheaded nova can dive into the action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T14:19:30-08:00","id":376612,"title":"","content":"<i>Very</i> interested to see how this works, Neall. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T00:01:31-08:00","id":377861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/375990-space-combat?p=376355#post376355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that space battles are better suited to fighter combat is something we tried to take into account for Codename: Sardonyx, and I think the scaling rules work <i>really</i> well. Capital ship combat should feel appreciably different from snubfighter dogfights, while the occasion hotheaded nova can dive into the action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to it!<br /> <br /> In my current game I'm running team of psions with a corvette, a class of ship that doesn't technically exist in the setting material, which I handwaved a bit about having a prototype second-generation jump drive. As when I read all there was about the jump drive and the associated leviathan ships I realized giving the PCs a massive ship was a terrible idea especially when everything about the game is <i>new</i> to them. Also made a few tables to serve as the random schema for the jump drive and its effects.<br /> <br /> Now for handling space combat with a non-fighter ship I converted another game's basic space combat rules to Trinity. And so far that has worked well for the two space battles that I've had over the last few months. I have personally taken the option that the space battles should be rare spectacles. Considering both the lethality of such battles and the cost of ship repairs. For amusement sake the little corvette I mentioned (the Mariner) took two structure levels of damage in the last battle and because neither Trinity or Orgotek was going to float the bill on this one the PCs were a tad stunned to discover they would have to acquire 100,000 yuans to pay for one of the structure levels to be repaired. The Legion would be covering the other one because they did help protect the convoy they where in.<br /> <br /> I admit seeing the shock and all the internal calculations they were doing about their salvage was rather amusing. Even considering selling some of their fuel (water) for money, although I got a leery look from one player for only giving a market value of 500 yuans to 1 ton of water out in the asteroid belt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}